{
  "$schema": "https://schema.management.azure.com/schemas/2019-04-01/deploymentTemplate.json#",
  "contentVersion": "1.0.0.0",
  "resources": [
    {
      "type": "Microsoft.Logic/workflows",
      "apiVersion": "2019-05-01",
      "name": "EmailQueueWriter",
      "location": "[resourceGroup().location]",
      "properties": {
        "definition": {
          "$schema": "https://schema.management.azure.com/providers/Microsoft.Logic/schemas/2016-06-01/workflowDefinition.json#",
          "actions": {
            "Create_SharePoint_Item": {
              "inputs": {
                "host": {
                  "connection": {
                    "name": "@parameters('connections')['sharepointonline']['connectionId']"
                  }
                },
                "method": "post",
                "path": "/datasets/default/tables/<YourListName>/items",
                "body": {
                  "fields": {
                    "Title": "@triggerBody()?['title']",
                    "To": "@triggerBody()?['to']",
                    "Body": "@triggerBody()?['body']",
                    "SourceApp": "@triggerBody()?['sourceApp']"
                  }
                }
              },
              "runAfter": {},
              "type": "ApiConnection"
            }
          },
          "triggers": {
            "manual": {
              "type": "Request",
              "kind": "Http",
              "inputs": {
                "schema": {
                  "type": "object",
                  "properties": {
                    "title": { "type": "string" },
                    "to": { "type": "string" },
                    "body": { "type": "string" },
                    "sourceApp": { "type": "string" }
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "outputs": {}
        },
        "parameters": {
          "connections": {
            "value": {
              "sharepointonline": {
                "connectionId": "<YOUR_SHAREPOINT_CONNECTION_ID>",
                "connectionName": "sharepointonline",
                "id": "/subscriptions/<sub-id>/resourceGroups/<rg-name>/providers/Microsoft.Web/connections/sharepointonline"
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}




  Notes
Replace REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_SECRET with your actual API key.

Replace <YourListName> with your SharePoint list's internal name.

Replace <sub-id>, <rg-name>, and the connectionId with real values from your environment.


example
curl -X POST https://<your-logic-app-url> \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -H "x-api-key: your-api-secret" \
  -d '{
        "title": "Test Email",
        "to": "someone@example.com",
        "body": "<p>Hello!</p>",
        "sourceApp": "AppA"
      }'

Create a New SharePoint Connection (manually)
If it doesn’t exist, create one:

Open your Logic App in Azure Portal

Go to the Designer

Add a step: SharePoint > Create item

You will be prompted to sign in to SharePoint

After successful sign-in, Azure will automatically create a sharepointonline connection in your subscription

📝 This connection is now a managed resource, and you can reuse it.



 Create SharePoint Connection via ARM Template
If you want to automate creation using IaC (ARM/Bicep), here’s how:

🔧 ARM Template Snippet
json
Copy
Edit
{
  "type": "Microsoft.Web/connections",
  "apiVersion": "2016-06-01",
  "name": "sharepointonline",
  "location": "global",
  "properties": {
    "displayName": "SharePoint Online",
    "api": {
      "id": "[concat('/subscriptions/', subscription().subscriptionId, '/providers/Microsoft.Web/locations/', parameters('location'), '/managedApis/sharepointonline')]"
    },
    "parameterValues": {
      "token:clientId": "<your-client-id>",
      "token:clientSecret": "<your-client-secret>",
      "token:tenantId": "<your-tenant-id>",
      "token:resourceUri": "https://graph.microsoft.com"
    }
  }
}
